'''''Lotus conimbricensis''''' has a trailing plant in the genus ''[[Lotus (genus)|Lotus]].''

this species is also known in Arabic as  לוֹטוּס רִיסָנִי.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Lotus conimbricensis Brot. {{!}} Flora of Israel and adjuscent areas |url=https://flora.org.il/en/plants/lotcon/?__cf_chl_tk=agqoXqGDb6Vz8tp_c5GnUFkW7uWqEQnIDzBQ6gqn3hQ-1737492538-1.0.1.1-m9xWl83OIIEWHTK5V3Bl27EBzKPyeGuQXCvHTGLyszI |access-date=2025-01-21 |website=צמחיית ישראל וסביבתה |language=en-US}}</ref>

== Appearance ==
''Lotus conimbricensis'' is identified by its singular white flower pea shaped flowers looking much like ''[[Lotus micranthus]]'' except with purple veining. This species also has hairs on the bottom and a smooth top of the small oval leaves which is a key identification feature.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Lotus conimbricensis Brot. – BIODIVERSITY OF LIBYA |url=https://biodiversity.ly/product/lotus-conimbricensis-brot/ |access-date=2024-08-07 |language=en-US}}</ref>

== Recognition ==
This species is recognized under the USDA PLANTS database.<ref>{{Cite web |title=USDA Plants Database |url=https://plants.usda.gov/home/classification/79988 |access-date=2024-08-07 |website=plants.usda.gov}}</ref>

== Status ==
This plant is considered least concern.

